(The main text ends on or before the page holding the "References" heading. These are camera-ready versions, which may use 10 pages; the submission limit is 9. Algorithm boxes are not counted as tables.)

- **Page use**: all fill the page budget; 0-5 figures (median 2) and 0-3 tables (median 1) in the main text; figures plus tables 2-6 (median 2). More floats than that is outside what this audience's accepted papers carry in the main text. Appendices run from none to about 11 pages.
- **Prior work**: 25-66 references, median 38. Related work is a paragraph or sub-subsection inside the introduction in 5 of 7, a separate Section 2 in 1 (Bandits), a late section in 1 (Embeddings).
- **Abstract** (169-266 words, median 192): (1) one or two sentences placing the problem in online platforms/experiments and naming interference as the obstacle; (2) the gap in existing methods ("all existing approaches require...", "far less is known"); (3) what the paper does, in plain terms, with the key technical device; (4) results: theory statements and "extensive simulations demonstrate...". None of the seven states a measured number. For this study, a measured abstract that states the main quantified finding and its scope is stronger than the sample's habit.
- **Introduction** (about 1.5-2 pages, roughly 700-1,650 words by extraction): motivation from online experimentation and social platforms; standard SUTVA failure and the bias of difference-in-means; the estimand (total/global treatment effect); what existing designs/estimators do and where they fall short; what the paper does; an contribution paragraph (labelled "Contributions" in 4 of 7, a contributions sentence in a fifth); related literature either inside the introduction or as the next section.
- **Experiments**: synthetic networks (SBM, Erdos-Renyi, power-law, random graphs) and, in at least 3 of 7, a real graph or a real platform case; comparisons against named baselines (difference-in-means, Horvitz-Thompson, Hajek, cluster-randomised variants); varied interference strength, density and model misspecification; tables with bias/SD/RMSE across settings or figures with error vs. a size parameter.
- **Limitations**: none of the seven has a stand-alone limitations section; they end with "Conclusion"/"Discussion". NeurIPS now asks for limitations in the checklist and reviewers are told not to penalise them, and the objective requires a limitations section, so the paper gives it its own section or clearly marked subsection.

## 5. Budget for the study (answering the outline's proposal)

Arithmetic (planning estimate, not a venue rule): 9 content pages of 9 in = 81 in of vertical text height. A full-width 5.5 in figure about 2.3 in tall with its caption takes about 2.9 in, roughly a third of a page; a table with caption takes 1.5-2.5 in.

- **Main text floats: up to 6 figures plus 2 tables** (each figure may be a multi-panel figure of up to 4 panels at 5.5 in width, panel text at least 7 pt printed). That is about 2.4 pages of floats and leaves about 6 pages for text. Beyond that the text drops below about 5.5 pages and the introduction, method and discussion get squeezed (planning judgement).
- The outline's proposal fits: main text Figs 1, 3, 5, 7 plus Tables 1-2 (4 figures, 2 tables, about 1.7 pages). Figs 2, 4, 6, 8 can join as extra panels or one extra multi-panel figure up to the cap of 6, or go to the appendix with a pointer sentence in the main text. Eight separate main-text figures plus two tables does not fit, and exceeds anything in the sample (max 5 figures).
- **Appendix**: no limit, text only in the same PDF (not a separate PDF, not in the ZIP). Use it for the cell list, calibration and sanity tables, derivations, full tables behind each figure, extra graph families. Keep each main-text claim self-contained.
- **Prior work**: aim at 35-60 references, all actually read; 25 is the lowest in the sample.
- **Abstract**: no venue limit known; **recommendation** at most about 220 words.
- **Introduction**: about 1.5 pages ending with an explicit contributions list that says what is not new (the brief's own requirement).
- Page counting is done from the built PDF of `paper-repo`: pages before the References heading must be at most 9 including every figure and table.
